        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303-a2">

                <pb facs="0552" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg424"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 36.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Count Hatzfeldt to
                        Mr. Kasson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-04-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 26,
                    1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned has the honor, while returning the inclosures of the note of the
                    22d August last, to inform the envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary
                    of the United States of America, Mr. John A. Kasson, that the name of David
                    Lemberger, now sojourning at Rexingen, has been stricken from the German
                    military rolls, it having been ascertained that he cannot be considered a
                    subject of the German Empire.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>v. HATZFELDT.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
